{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And Elohim blessed.</b> The meaning of \"blessing\" is an addition of good, and on this day there is renewed in bodies a likeness of generative power, and in souls the power of cognition and intellect." "\"And He sanctified it.\" For no work was done in it, unlike its companions." "And the meaning of \"which Elohim created to do\" is: the roots of all the species, in which He placed the power to produce their likeness. And the one who explains \"to do\" in place of \"He did,\" and \"He did\" in place of \"created\" — it is not so in my opinion. And the Gaon [Saadia] said that the blessing of the day and its holiness returns upon those who observe it, that they be blessed and holy:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:42:51.333305443Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}